WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.082
By the end of this module, you should be able to create and use standard views, inspect how they are defined,

00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:10.492
and understand what other objects they depend on.

00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:17.717
You should also be able to explain when a simple view can accept updates, what the with check option does,

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:21.312
and why a materialized view can become stale.

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:30.537
Most importantly, you should be able to choose among three tools: a common table expression for logic used inside one

00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:37.497
statement, a standard view for shared live logic, and a materialized view for a stored result that can be refreshed.
